{
  "$comment": [
    "pnpm check:contrast's colour pairs (scripts/check-contrast.ts): every pair in the colour tables of DESIGN §3.1 and §3.2, the accent presets on each surface, increased contrast (DESIGN §4.5), and the text and inspection colours on each surface they sit on.",
    "min is 3 for UI (the --line data lines) and 4.5 for text. stated is the ratio as DESIGN writes it, checked at that precision.",
    "A scope layers blocks of src/styles/tokens.css in order, a later block overriding an earlier one. Every block has the same specificity, so the order is the stylesheet's own.",
    "tests/e2e/contrast-cascade.spec.ts applies each scope to a page of the production build and checks that the browser computes the same colours.",
    "The workspace's dark theme is the public tokens (DESIGN §3.2), so the public pairs cover it. Data lines never sit on Daylight's --surface-3 (D-038), so that pair is not here.",
    "fg and bg are tokens, or a hex colour for a literal one such as white text."
  ],
  "scopes": {
    "public": [":root"],
    "public-more-contrast": [":root", "@media (prefers-contrast: more) :root"],
    "daylight": [":root", "[data-theme=\"daylight\"]"],
    "daylight-more-contrast": [
      ":root",
      "[data-theme=\"daylight\"]",
      "@media (prefers-contrast: more) :root",
      "@media (prefers-contrast: more) [data-theme=\"daylight\"]"
    ],
    "accent-electric_blue": [":root", "[data-accent=\"electric_blue\"]"],
    "accent-mint": [":root", "[data-accent=\"mint\"]"],
    "accent-ivory": [":root", "[data-accent=\"ivory\"]"],
    "accent-violet": [":root", "[data-accent=\"violet\"]"],
    "daylight-accent-mint": [":root", "[data-accent=\"mint\"]", "[data-theme=\"daylight\"]"]
  },
